### Super admin signin
# POST /super-admin/auth/signin
#
# Signs the super admin in and returns the JWT their later requests carry.
# Public, because this is one of the endpoints that hands a token out rather
# than asking for one.
#
# The role is fixed by the endpoint. An admin or an employee with correct
# credentials is still refused here, and a deactivated account cannot sign back
# in. An unknown username and a wrong password both answer 401, so neither can
# be used to discover which usernames exist.
#
# Only username and password are accepted. The schema rejects unknown fields,
# so sending user_type or role is a 400.
#
# Base url and path pieces come from the REST Client variables in
# .vscode/settings.json. Run super_admin_signup.http first if no account exists.
#
# Expect 200 with the account and a token. Copy that token into the
# super_admin_token variable in .vscode/settings.json to use it on the
# protected super admin routes.

POST {{localBase_url}}{{super_admin_route}}{{signin_route}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "superadmin",
  "password": "Airstone@123456"
}
